#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0333 expect=violation domain=PP
#note "S3 foreign discrimination (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3). Authority: SEND Conformance Rules v5.0 SEND333 (Condition: PC records contribute to a single time concentration profile in PP; Rule: PCNOMDY & PCTPTREF = PPNOMDY & PPTPTREF). Partially Executable (underreporting): the Check tests the PP pair against the study-wide set of PC pairs, not against the pair of that profile own PC records; here every silent PP row pairs with its OWN subject profile, so the unchecked association is not violated (plan §2.4). PCNOMDY / PPNOMDY are declared Num. Each subject has one PC profile and at most one PP profile, so the PC records of a subject contribute to that subject's PP profile and the Condition holds. Row 1 (S1-002) summarises S1-002's own PC profile, whose records carry the pair (28, Day 28 Dose), but reports (14, Day 14 Dose), the pair of no PC record -> fires. The primary PP deliberately carries PCNOMDY and PCTPTREF columns (PP normally has neither; the rule has no Requirements.Variables.None) holding that same pair (14, Day 14 Dose): a port that read [PCNOMDY, PCTPTREF] from the primary PP instead of the FOREIGN PC would find the row's own pair in its set and fall silent."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=S1-002 PPNOMDY=14 PPTPTREF="Day 14 Dose"
dataset PP class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Parameters"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PPSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PPTESTCD type=Char label="Parameter Short Name"
col PPNOMDY  type=Num  label="Nominal Study Day for Tabulations"
col PPTPTREF type=Char label="Time Point Reference"
col PCNOMDY  type=Num  label="Nominal Study Day for Tabulations"
col PCTPTREF type=Char label="Time Point Reference"
---
S1 | PP | S1-002 | 1 | CMAX | 14 | Day 14 Dose | 14 | Day 14 Dose
---

dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCNOMDY  type=Num  label="Nominal Study Day for Tabulations"
col PCTPTREF type=Char label="Time Point Reference"
col PCTPTNUM type=Num  label="Planned Time Point Number"
---
S1 | PC | S1-001 | 1 | DRUGX | 1  | Day 1 Dose  | 1
S1 | PC | S1-001 | 2 | DRUGX | 1  | Day 1 Dose  | 2
S1 | PC | S1-002 | 1 | DRUGX | 28 | Day 28 Dose | 1
S1 | PC | S1-002 | 2 | DRUGX | 28 | Day 28 Dose | 2
---
